Z||000007||William||02-23-2000||12:21 AM||||84 - 85 coupe nose. I spent some time finding a Fiero with a V-6, 4 speed, and the original pointy nose( 85 SE is the only model with this combo apparently), I guess this is because that facia always reminded me of the exotic cars of the 70's/ 80's that I grew up dreaming about.||||reg||14
Z||000008||DJRice||02-23-2000||08:49 AM||||I like the aero nose, but I think that an 85 SE with the sixer would be cool too.  I like the looks of both.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ChadMan||02-23-2000||09:03 AM||||All Fiero noses are beautiful.  But one thing's for sure - a front license plate doesn't ruin the looks of the 84-86 Coupe nose the way it ruins the aero and Formula noses.  I hate the "tacked-on" look of the front plate on my 88 Coupe.  Stupid Ohio laws.||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||02-23-2000||11:59 AM||||I agree ChadMan. I don't like the front plate on my 87 coupe either. But the 87-88 coupe/Formula nose is my favorite. I think it has a Euro look to it. Don't get me wrong I like all Fiero body configurations. If I had my dream Fiero it would be a 88 Formula with a GTA style spoiler !||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||02-23-2000||01:54 PM||||I like the 87-88 coupe/Formula better than the 84-86 coupe. I think it's mostly that I prefer the all body color to the black "pads".||||reg||1
